var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"location":"examples/2d-elliptic-bkw/#2D-Elliptical-BKW-walkthrough","page":"Examples/2D Elliptic BKW","title":"2D Elliptical BKW walkthrough","text":"This page is a walkthrough of examples/2D_run_lenardbalescu_demo_elliptical_bkw.jl. It explains what the script does, in order, and how to modify it.","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/2d-elliptic-bkw/#What-this-example-is","page":"Examples/2D Elliptic BKW","title":"What this example is","text":"Operator: 2D Lenard–Balescu (use_lenard_balescu=true)\nSymmetry mode: non-radial / elliptical BKW (radial_symmetry=false by default in the script)\nInitial condition: stratified elliptical BKW (initialize_particles_stratified_BKW_elliptical)\nEntry point function: run_lenardbalescu_animation_elliptical_bkw\n\nThe script calls the convenience wrapper at the bottom, so running the file executes the demo immediately.","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/2d-elliptic-bkw/#Step-1-—-Run-it-as-provided","page":"Examples/2D Elliptic BKW","title":"Step 1 — Run it as provided","text":"From the repository root:\n\njulia --project -e 'include(\"examples/2D_run_lenardbalescu_demo_elliptical_bkw.jl\")'\n\nThis runs the convenience call at the end (the file uses longer defaults suitable for producing full output).","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/2d-elliptic-bkw/#Step-2-—-Understand-the-flow-inside-the-function","page":"Examples/2D Elliptic BKW","title":"Step 2 — Understand the flow inside the function","text":"run_lenardbalescu_animation_elliptical_bkw does the following:\n\nCreates RNG and parameters (rng = MersenneTwister(seed), par = SetParam()).\nConfigures 2D discretization and timing (par.dim = 2, par.Nv, par.Npc, par.dt, par.ntot, par.T).\nSets Lenard–Balescu k-space controls (par.k_perp_order, par.k_perp_max, par.k_parallel_width, par.k_parallel_order) and calls update_kernel_params!(par).\nOptionally builds an initial f_grid and radial diagnostics for plotting when plot_grid=true.\nPrepares output folders and a frames array if PNGs/animation are requested.\nDefines a visualization_callback(k, vstack, wg, par, Vgrid, Vc) which:\ncomputes conserved quantities and appends to mass_hist, energy_hist, momentum_hist;\nreconstructs f_grid = f_recon(...);\nwhen plot_grid=true it builds a four-panel diagnostic: particle scatter, density heatmap, radial binned f(r), and radial derivative plots;\nsaves per-step PNG frames and collects them for a GIF.\nCalls run_simulation(...) with:\nuse_lenard_balescu=true\ninit_particles=(N, dV, Vgrid, par, rng) -> initialize_particles_stratified_BKW_elliptical(...)\nvisualization callback attached and trackconserved=true.\nAfter the run, assembles conserved/error plots, saves PNG summaries, and — if requested — writes a GIF from saved frames.","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/2d-elliptic-bkw/#Step-3-—-Run-a-quicker-variant-interactively","page":"Examples/2D Elliptic BKW","title":"Step 3 — Run a quicker variant interactively","text":"For iteration and development, run with fewer timesteps and smaller kernels:\n\nusing LenardBalescu\ninclude(\"examples/2D_run_lenardbalescu_demo_elliptical_bkw.jl\")\n\nrun_lenardbalescu_animation_elliptical_bkw(\n    ntot=60,\n    seed=1,\n    batchsize=0,\n    stretch=1.5,\n    save_pngs=false,\n    plot_grid=true\n)\n\nThis reduces walltime while keeping the visualization pipeline intact.","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/2d-elliptic-bkw/#Step-4-—-What-to-modify-(and-what-each-knob-changes)","page":"Examples/2D Elliptic BKW","title":"Step 4 — What to modify (and what each knob changes)","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/2d-elliptic-bkw/#Initial-condition-/-geometry","page":"Examples/2D Elliptic BKW","title":"Initial condition / geometry","text":"stretch: stretches the BKW distribution into an ellipse — increase to accentuate anisotropy.\nThe initializer is provided inline via the init_particles lambda that calls initialize_particles_stratified_BKW_elliptical.","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/2d-elliptic-bkw/#Runtime-and-cost","page":"Examples/2D Elliptic BKW","title":"Runtime and cost","text":"ntot: number of timesteps (dominant runtime factor).\nbatchsize: RBM batching size; set to 0 for full pairwise collision (slower but exact), or to a positive integer to enable RBM batching and reduce cost.\npar.Nv, par.Npc: change particle/discretization resolution — increasing increases accuracy and cost.","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/2d-elliptic-bkw/#Lenard–Balescu-fidelity-controls","page":"Examples/2D Elliptic BKW","title":"Lenard–Balescu fidelity controls","text":"par.k_perp_order, par.k_perp_max, par.k_parallel_width, par.k_parallel_order control quadrature and k-space coverage. Higher values improve accuracy but increase kernel-precompute and collision cost.","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/2d-elliptic-bkw/#Output-and-visualization","page":"Examples/2D Elliptic BKW","title":"Output and visualization","text":"save_pngs: toggle per-step PNG saving (used to create the GIF).\nplot_grid: toggle the diagnostic panel construction.\nout_gif, out_dir: file locations for GIF and frames.","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/2d-elliptic-bkw/#Practical-notes","page":"Examples/2D Elliptic BKW","title":"Practical notes","text":"The convenience call at the bottom auto-runs a long example. Comment it out for library-style usage and call the function yourself with smaller parameters when developing.\nThe example uses initialize_particles_stratified_BKW_elliptical which seeds particles with stratified sampling — change to another initializer for different starting distributions.\nWhen batchsize==0 the example runs the full pairwise collision operator (highest fidelity); try modest batchsize values to trade accuracy for speed during exploration.","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/2d-elliptic-bkw/#Relevant-files","page":"Examples/2D Elliptic BKW","title":"Relevant files","text":"Example script: examples/2D_run_lenardbalescu_demo_elliptical_bkw.jl\nInitializer: initialize_particles_stratified_BKW_elliptical (see src/init_particles.jl)\nSimulation core: run_simulation (see src/simulate.jl)","category":"section"},{"location":"api/#API","page":"API","title":"API","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.LenardBalescu","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.LenardBalescu","text":"LenardBalescu\n\nA Julia package for Lenard-Balescu (and Landau) collision operator physics simulations.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"module"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.BasisKernel","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.BasisKernel","text":"BasisKernel(order::Int, e::Float64)\n\nBasis function descriptor for particle-in-cell (PIC) velocity mesh coupling.\n\nSupports multiple basis function orders:\n\n0: Gaussian kernel\n1: Linear B-spline\n2: Quadratic B-spline\n3: Cubic B-spline\n\nEach basis function ψ and its gradient ∇ψ are used to map between particles and the velocity grid.\n\nArguments\n\norder: Kernel order (0=Gaussian, 1=linear, 2=quadratic, 3=cubic)\ne: Kernel scale parameter (Gaussian width parameter; dilation scale for B-splines)\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.Params","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.Params","text":"Params\n\nSimulation parameters for Lenard-Balescu or Landau kinetic equation simulations.\n\nFields\n\ngam, beta, c, temp, m: Kernel and physical parameters.\nLv, Nv, Npc, N: Velocity grid parameters.\nT, dt, ntot: Time stepping parameters.\nbatchsize: RBM target batch size (0 disables batching; default full interaction).   In RBM mode, particles are repartitioned each step into balanced batches. For   2 <= batchsize < N, this can still reduce cost even when batchsize is close   to N (for example, it may produce two roughly equal batches and reduce pair   work from about N^2 to about N^2/2).\nspline_order, use_cell_list: Spline and collision parameters.\nepsi, cell_h: Derived parameters (set by update_kernel_params!).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.B2-Tuple{Float64}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.B2","text":"B2(x::Float64)\n\nQuadratic B-spline basis function (order=2).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.B3-Tuple{Float64}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.B3","text":"B3(x::Float64)\n\nCubic B-spline basis function (order=3).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.BKW_vector-Tuple{Float64, Float64, Float64, Float64, AbstractArray{Float64}}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.BKW_vector","text":"BKW_vector(t, T_tot, C_BKW, B_BKW, Vgrid)\n\nBobylev-Krook-Wu (BKW) exact solution for the homogeneous Boltzmann equation on a 2D velocity grid.\n\nArguments\n\nt: Time\nT_tot: Total temperature\nC_BKW: Amplitude parameter\nB_BKW: Decay rate\nVgrid: 2D tensor grid of velocity-cell centres, with components stored in the last dimension\n\nReturns\n\nM-vector of distribution-function values\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.Collision","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.Collision","text":"Collision(vstack, par, wg, elapsed_s=nothing;\n          Vgrid=nothing, use_lenard_balescu=true, verbose=0,\n          radial_symmetry=true,\n          dielectric_r0, dielectric_dr,\n          dielectric_inv_dr, dielectric_len)\n\nLenard-Balescu (or Landau) collision operator for particle velocities.\n\nArguments\n\nvstack: N×dim particle velocities (dim = par.dim, supports 2 or 3)\npar: Simulation parameters\nwg: Particle weights\nelapsed_s: (optional) Ref for computation time\nVgrid: (optional) velocity grid used for reconstruction/precomputation\nuse_lenard_balescu: Use Lenard-Balescu (true) or Landau (false)\nverbose: Verbosity level\nradial_symmetry: Controls dielectric preprocessing mode for Lenard-Balescu\ndielectric_r0: Precomputed interpolation-grid origin (first grid value)\ndielectric_dr: Precomputed interpolation-grid spacing\ndielectric_inv_dr: Precomputed inverse spacing (1/dr) for fast indexing\ndielectric_len: Precomputed interpolation-grid length\n\nReturns\n\nN×dim matrix of collision derivatives (dv/dt)\n\nNotes\n\nLandau path supports dim = 2 and dim = 3.\nLenard-Balescu path supports dim = 2 and dim = 3 in both radial   (radial_symmetry=true) and generic (radial_symmetry=false) modes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.G1-Tuple{Float64}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.G1","text":"G1(x::Float64)\n\nLinear B-spline (hat) function: triangular support, linear falloff (order=1).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.L1_error-Tuple{AbstractVector{Float64}, AbstractVector{Float64}, Float64}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.L1_error","text":"L1_error(a::AbstractVector{Float64}, b::AbstractVector{Float64}, dV::Float64; dim::Int=2)\n\nComputes the L1 error (sum of absolute differences) between two distributions on a 2D or 3D grid.\n\nArguments\n\na, b: Vectors of distribution values (must be same length)\ndV: Grid cell width\ndim: Velocity-space dimension used in volume scaling (dV^dim, default 2)\n\nReturns\n\nL1 error as a Float64\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.L2_error-Tuple{AbstractVector{Float64}, AbstractVector{Float64}, Float64}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.L2_error","text":"L2_error(a::AbstractVector{Float64}, b::AbstractVector{Float64}, dV::Float64; dim::Int=2)\n\nComputes the L2 error norm between two distributions on a 2D or 3D grid.\n\nArguments\n\na, b: Vectors of distribution values (must be same length)\ndV: Grid cell width\ndim: Velocity-space dimension used in volume scaling (dV^dim, default 2)\n\nReturns\n\nL2 error as a Float64\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.SetParam-Tuple{}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.SetParam","text":"SetParam()\n\nCreate and initialize a Params struct with default simulation parameters for Lenard-Balescu or Landau kinetic equation simulations.\n\nThis function sets up the default grid, time, and kernel parameters, computes derived quantities, and ensures consistency between fields.\n\nReturns\n\nA fully initialized Params struct with all fields set to default values.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.build_velocity_grid-Tuple{Params}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.build_velocity_grid","text":"build_velocity_grid(par::Params)\n\nConstruct a 2D or 3D velocity grid for the simulation.\n\nArguments\n\npar::Params: Simulation parameters, must contain Lv (velocity limit), Nv (number of grid cells per dimension), and dim (2 or 3).\n\nReturns\n\nV: Vector of velocity grid edges\ndV: Grid cell width\nVc: Vector of velocity grid cell centers\nVgrid: Tensor grid of velocity-cell centres, with component index in the last dimension\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.collision_pairwise_subset-Tuple{AbstractMatrix{Float64}, Params, AbstractVector{Float64}, AbstractVector{Float64}, AbstractVector{Float64}, Union{Nothing, AbstractVector{Float64}}, AbstractVector{Int64}, AbstractVector{Int64}}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.collision_pairwise_subset","text":"collision_pairwise_subset(vstack, par, wg, Fx, Fy, Fz, idx_i, idx_j;\n                          use_lenard_balescu=true,\n                          kernel_state=nothing)\n\nEvaluate only the pairwise interaction stage for particle indices idx_i against idx_j using precomputed global fields.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.component_grid_views-Tuple{AbstractArray{Float64}, Params}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.component_grid_views","text":"component_grid_views(Vgrid::AbstractArray{Float64}, par::Params)\n\nReturn a tuple of component-wise views of Vgrid along its last dimension.\n\nFor par.dim == 2, returns (Vx, Vy); for par.dim == 3, returns (Vx, Vy, Vz).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.compute_collision_fields-Tuple{AbstractMatrix{Float64}, Params, AbstractVector{Float64}}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.compute_collision_fields","text":"compute_collision_fields(vstack, par, wg)\n\nCompute the global advection fields (Fx, Fy, Fz) used by the collision operator. This includes the cell-list-accelerated f_tilde/denom/F stages and is intended to be evaluated on the full particle set.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.compute_conserved_quantities-Tuple{AbstractMatrix{Float64}, AbstractVector{Float64}, Params}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.compute_conserved_quantities","text":"compute_conserved_quantities(vstack, wg, par)\n\nCompute total mass, momentum (as a vector), and energy from particle velocities and weights.\n\nArguments\n\nvstack: N×dim matrix of particle velocities (dim = par.dim, supports 2 or 3)\nwg: Vector of particle weights\npar: Simulation parameters (must have field m for particle mass)\n\nReturns\n\nNamed tuple with fields:\n\nmass: Total mass (sum of weights)\nmomentum: Total momentum vector (2 or 3 components depending on par.dim)\nenergy: Total kinetic energy (sum of weighted 0.5*m*|v|^2)\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.compute_dielectric_response!","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.compute_dielectric_response!","text":"compute_dielectric_response!(dielectric_sq, k_nodes, v_parallel,\n                             G, HG, r, I_integral, dim=2)\n\nCompute dielectric-response magnitude squared at each k-sample using precomputed profiles G, HG on a uniform lookup grid r.\n\nArguments\n\ndielectric_sq: Output array, updated in-place\nk_nodes: k magnitudes\nv_parallel: Parallel velocity samples corresponding to k_nodes\nG, HG: Precomputed profile arrays on r\nr: Uniform lookup grid used for interpolation\nI_integral: Normalization integral used in radial mode\ndim: Dimension (2 or 3)\n\nReturns\n\nThe updated dielectric_sq array\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.compute_entropy-Tuple{AbstractVector, Float64}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.compute_entropy","text":"compute_entropy(f_grid, dV; dim=2)\n\nCompute entropy from a distribution f_grid and grid spacing dV.\n\nArguments\n\nf_grid: Smoothed distribution values on the velocity grid\ndV: Grid spacing in one velocity dimension\ndim: Velocity-space dimension used for volume scaling (dV^dim)\n\nReturns\n\nApproximated entropy value S = ∫ f log(f) dV.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.compute_hilbert_transform-Tuple{AbstractVector, AbstractVector}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.compute_hilbert_transform","text":"compute_hilbert_transform(x::AbstractVector, y::AbstractVector)\n\nCompute Hilbert transform of y(x) via DSP.jl's FFT-based algorithm.\n\nThe Hilbert transform is: H[y](x) = (1/π) ∫ y(t)/(x-t) dt Implementation pads signal to next power of 2 for FFT efficiency.\n\nArguments\n\nx: Grid points (must be uniformly spaced for FFT)\ny: Function values at grid points\n\nReturns\n\nH_y::Vector: Hilbert transform values (same length as y)\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.compute_lenard_balescu_kernel!-Tuple{Float64, Float64, Float64, Float64, Float64, AbstractArray, AbstractArray, Float64, Float64, Float64, Float64, Int64, Vararg{AbstractMatrix, 8}}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.compute_lenard_balescu_kernel!","text":"compute_lenard_balescu_kernel!(r, vx_i, vy_i, vx_j, vy_j,\n                               G, HG, I_integral,\n                               r0, dr, inv_dr, len_r,\n                               k_parallel, k_perp, norm_k, approx,\n                               phi_p_11, phi_p_22, phi_p_12)\n\nFused kernel: computes rotated k-vectors, dielectric response, and kernel tensor in a single pass over the k-space grid.\n\nReturns the symmetric 2×2 tensor entries (Kxx, Kxy, Kyy) for the 2D Lenard-Balescu path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.compute_lenard_balescu_kernel_3d!-Tuple{Float64, Float64, Float64, Float64, Float64, Float64, Float64, AbstractArray, AbstractArray, Float64, Float64, Float64, Float64, Int64, Vararg{AbstractVector, 6}}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.compute_lenard_balescu_kernel_3d!","text":"compute_lenard_balescu_kernel_3d!(...)\n\nCompute the 3×3 Lenard-Balescu kernel tensor in 3D using precomputed k-space samples in a local frame aligned with v_i - v_j.\n\nReturns the 9 tensor entries in row-major order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.compute_radial_binned_f-Tuple{AbstractVector, AbstractArray{Float64}, Params}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.compute_radial_binned_f","text":"compute_radial_binned_f(f_grid::AbstractVector, Vgrid::AbstractMatrix, par::Params; n_bins::Int=15)\n\nCompute radially binned 1D distribution f(r) from a 2D or 3D velocity grid representation. Uses unsigned radius r = ||v|| and averages f within radial shells.\n\nReturns (r_plot, f_plot) on a symmetric radial axis [-r_max, r_max].\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.compute_radial_binned_f-Tuple{AbstractVector, AbstractVector, Params}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.compute_radial_binned_f","text":"compute_radial_binned_f(f_grid::AbstractVector, Vc::AbstractVector, par::Params; n_bins::Int=15)\n\nCompatibility 2D wrapper for radial binning from 1D center coordinates Vc. This method is defined for par.dim == 2 and forwards to the (f_grid, Vgrid, par) method after constructing a 2D Vgrid.\n\nReturns (rcenters, fbinned) where:\n\nrcenters: bin center positions (ranges from 0 to rmax)\nf_binned: averaged f values within each bin\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.compute_radial_integral_G","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.compute_radial_integral_G","text":"compute_radial_integral_G(x::Float64, r::AbstractVector, f_prime::AbstractVector, dim::Int=2)\n\nCompute the radial integral G(x) for the computed Hilbert transform.\n\nFor radially symmetric distributions:     G(x) = S{d-2} ∫{|x|}^{∞} f'(r) (r² - x²)^{(d-3)/2} dr\n\nwhere S_{d-2} is the surface area of unit sphere in d-1 dimensions.\n\nArguments\n\nx: Evaluation point (typically v_parallel)\nr: Radial grid points (must be sorted)\nf_prime: Derivative values on radial grid\ndim: Dimension (2 or 3)\n\nReturns\n\nG_x::Float64: Value of G at x\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.convolve_hat_at_point-Tuple{AbstractVector, AbstractVector, Vararg{Float64, 4}}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.convolve_hat_at_point","text":"convolve_hat_at_point(r::AbstractVector, G::AbstractVector, v::Float64, width::Float64,\n                      r0::Float64, dr::Float64)\n\nReturn discrete convolution of G(r) with the triangular hat kernel of half-width width evaluated at v. Assumes r is uniformly spaced with spacing dr and origin r0.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.dB2-Tuple{Float64}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.dB2","text":"dB2(x::Float64)\n\nDerivative of the quadratic B-spline basis function.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.dB3-Tuple{Float64}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.dB3","text":"dB3(x::Float64)\n\nDerivative of the cubic B-spline basis function.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.dG1-Tuple{Float64}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.dG1","text":"dG1(x::Float64)\n\nDerivative of the linear B-spline (hat) function.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.extract_uniform_axis_spacing-Tuple{AbstractArray{Float64}}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.extract_uniform_axis_spacing","text":"extract_uniform_axis_spacing(vals::AbstractArray{Float64}) -> (v0::Float64, dv::Float64)\n\nExtract the origin and uniform spacing from a velocity grid axis array.\n\nReads all unique values from vals, validates that they form a uniformly-spaced sequence, and returns the minimum value and the spacing.\n\nArguments\n\nvals: Array of grid coordinates for one velocity axis (may be multi-dimensional).\n\nReturns\n\nv0: Minimum coordinate value (grid origin for that axis).\ndv: Uniform grid spacing.\n\nErrors\n\nThrows an error if fewer than 2 unique values are found, if the spacing is not positive and finite, or if the axis is not uniformly spaced.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.f_recon-Tuple{AbstractMatrix{Float64}, AbstractVector{Float64}, AbstractArray{Float64}, Params}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.f_recon","text":"f_recon(vstack, wg, Vgrid, par)\n\nReconstructs the distribution function on a velocity grid from particle positions and weights.\n\nArguments\n\nvstack: particle-velocity matrix (one particle per row; columns follow par.dim)\nwg: Particle weights\nVgrid: tensor grid of velocity-cell centres, with component index in the last dimension\npar: Simulation parameters\n\nReturns\n\n1D array of reconstructed distribution values on the grid\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.fit_bspline-Tuple{AbstractVector, AbstractVector}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.fit_bspline","text":"fit_bspline(r_centers, f_binned)\n\nFit a cubic B-spline interpolation to sampled 1D data.\n\nReturns spline metadata and callable interpolation/derivative functions with flat extrapolation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.flatten_row_major-Tuple{AbstractArray{Float64}}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.flatten_row_major","text":"flatten_row_major(arr::AbstractArray{Float64})\n\nConvert an N-D array of Float64 values to a 1D vector in row-major order (last index varies fastest).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.gauss_legendre_quadrature-Tuple{Int64, Float64, Float64}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.gauss_legendre_quadrature","text":"gauss_legendre_quadrature(n::Int, a::Float64, b::Float64)\n\nCompute Gauss-Legendre quadrature nodes and weights on interval [a, b].\n\nArguments\n\nn: Number of quadrature points\na, b: Integration interval endpoints\n\nReturns\n\nnodes::Vector: Quadrature nodes\nweights::Vector: Quadrature weights\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.getA_Landau-NTuple{6, Float64}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.getA_Landau","text":"getA_Landau(vxi::Float64, vyi::Float64, vxj::Float64, vyj::Float64, g::Float64, beta::Float64)\n\nCompute the four elements of the collision kernel matrix A for a velocity pair using the Landau operator.\n\nArguments\n\nvxi, vyi: Components of the first particle's velocity.\nvxj, vyj: Components of the second particle's velocity.\ng: Exponent parameter for the velocity difference.\nbeta: Scaling parameter for the kernel.\n\nReturns\n\naxL, axR, ayL, ayR: The four elements of the collision kernel matrix A as a tuple.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.getA_Landau_3D-NTuple{8, Float64}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.getA_Landau_3D","text":"getA_Landau_3D(vxi, vyi, vzi, vxj, vyj, vzj, g, beta)\n\nCompute the 3×3 Landau tensor for a velocity pair in 3D:\n\nA = beta * |q|^g * (|q|^2 I - q q^T),   q = v_i - v_j\n\nReturns the 9 tensor entries in row-major order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.hat-Tuple{AbstractVector, Float64}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.hat","text":"hat(x::AbstractVector, eps::Float64)\n\nTriangular hat function used to approximate delta in k_parallel.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.initialize_particles_maxwellian","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.initialize_particles_maxwellian","text":"initialize_particles_maxwellian(N, par, rng)\n\nInitialize N particles with velocities sampled independently from a Maxwellian distribution with temperature par.temp.\n\nArguments\n\nN: Total number of particles\npar: Simulation parameters (must contain temp and dim)\nrng: (optional) random number generator\n\nReturns\n\n(vstack, wg) where vstack is N×2 for par.dim == 2 and N×3 for par.dim == 3\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.initialize_particles_spherical_shell_3d","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.initialize_particles_spherical_shell_3d","text":"initialize_particles_spherical_shell_3d(N, par, rng; shell_radius=2.0, thickness=0.3)\n\nInitialize N particles in 3D velocity space inside a spherical shell centered at the origin. The shell has mean radius shell_radius and radial thickness thickness.\n\nSampling is uniform in shell volume, with radius distributed over [shell_radius - thickness/2, shell_radius + thickness/2] and isotropic direction.\n\nArguments\n\nN: Total number of particles\npar: Simulation parameters (must have dim == 3)\nrng: Random number generator\nshell_radius: Mean shell radius\nthickness: Shell thickness (must be > 0)\n\nReturns\n\n(vstack, wg) with vstack shaped N×3 and uniform particle weights\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.initialize_particles_stratified_BKW","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.initialize_particles_stratified_BKW","text":"initialize_particles_stratified_BKW(vx, vy, wg, N, dV, Vgrid, par, [rng])\n\nStratified initialization of N particles from the BKW distribution on a 2D velocity grid.\n\nArguments\n\nvx, vy, wg: Preallocated vectors to be filled with particle velocities and weights\nN: Total number of particles\ndV: Grid cell width\nVgrid: matrix of velocity-grid cell centres (one centre per row), from build_velocity_grid\npar: Simulation parameters (must contain temp, c, beta)\nrng: (optional) random number generator\n\nReturns\n\n(vstack, wg) after copying the generated particles into the supplied vectors\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.initialize_particles_stratified_BKW_elliptical","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.initialize_particles_stratified_BKW_elliptical","text":"initialize_particles_stratified_BKW_elliptical(N, dV, Vgrid, par, [rng]; stretch=2.0)\n\nStratified initialization of N particles from a BKW distribution stretched along the x axis (elliptical shape).\n\nArguments\n\nN: Total number of particles\ndV: Grid cell width\nVgrid: matrix of velocity-grid cell centres (one centre per row), from build_velocity_grid\npar: Simulation parameters (must contain temp, c, beta)\nrng: (optional) random number generator\nstretch: Stretch factor along x axis (default: 2.0)\n\nReturns\n\n(vstack, wg) where vstack is N×2\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.initialize_particles_stratified_double_ring","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.initialize_particles_stratified_double_ring","text":"initialize_particles_stratified_double_ring(N, dV, Vgrid, par, [rng]; ...)\n\nStratified initialization of N particles from two concentric Gaussian rings (and optional central Maxwellian) in velocity space.\n\nArguments\n\nN: Total number of particles\ndV: Grid cell width\nVgrid: matrix of velocity-grid cell centres (one centre per row), from build_velocity_grid\npar: Simulation parameters (must contain temp)\nrng: (optional) random number generator\ninclude_bulk: Whether to include a central Maxwellian (default: true)\nring1_fraction, ring2_fraction: Fractions of total density in each ring (default: 0.15)\nring1_radius, ring2_radius: Radial positions of the rings (default: 1.3, 2.7)\nring1_width, ring2_width: Widths (standard deviation) of the rings (default: 0.15)\n\nReturns\n\n(vstack, wg) where vstack is N×dim\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.initialize_particles_stratified_maxwellian","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.initialize_particles_stratified_maxwellian","text":"initialize_particles_stratified_maxwellian(N, dV, Vgrid, par, rng)\n\nStratified initialization of N particles from a Maxwellian distribution on a 2D or 3D velocity grid.\n\nThis method distributes particles uniformly across grid cells according to local Maxwellian weights. It produces better coverage than random sampling for low-N simulations, but particles do not form a true random sample. Expect a brief relaxation transient (typically < few collision times) as the ensemble evolves toward a true Maxwellian. For transient-free equilibrium initialization, use initialize_particles_maxwellian instead.\n\nArguments\n\nN: Total number of particles\ndV: Grid cell width\nVgrid: matrix of velocity-grid cell centres (one centre per row), from build_velocity_grid\npar: Simulation parameters (must contain temp, dim, Lv)\nrng: (optional) random number generator\n\nReturns\n\n(vstack, wg) where vstack is N×2 or N×3 matrix (2D or 3D) and wg is weights\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.initialize_particles_torus_3d","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.initialize_particles_torus_3d","text":"initialize_particles_torus_3d(N, par, rng; major_radius=2.0, tube_radius=0.35)\n\nInitialize N particles in 3D velocity space on a solid torus centered on the z-axis, lying in the xy-plane. The torus major radius is major_radius and minor radius is tube_radius.\n\nArguments\n\nN: Total number of particles\npar: Simulation parameters (must have dim == 3)\nrng: Random number generator\nmajor_radius: Distance from origin to the centerline circle in the xy-plane\ntube_radius: Radius of the torus tube\n\nReturns\n\n(vstack, wg) with vstack shaped N×3 and uniform particle weights\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.partition_random_batches-Tuple{Random.AbstractRNG, Int64, Int64}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.partition_random_batches","text":"partition_random_batches(rng, N, batchsize)\n\nRandomly partition 1:N into balanced batches used by RBM acceleration.\n\nFor batchsize < 2 or batchsize >= N, returns a single batch containing all indices and redistributed_remainder = 0.\n\nReturns\n\nbatches::Vector{Vector{Int}}: random balanced partition of particle indices\nredistributed_remainder::Int: number of batches that received one extra index\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.precompute_collision_kernel_state-Tuple{AbstractMatrix{Float64}, Params, AbstractVector{Float64}}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.precompute_collision_kernel_state","text":"precompute_collision_kernel_state(vstack, par, wg;\n                                  Vgrid, use_lenard_balescu,\n                                  radial_symmetry,\n                                  dielectric_r0, dielectric_dr,\n                                  dielectric_inv_dr, dielectric_len)\n\nPrecompute data reused by pairwise collision evaluation. For Landau mode this returns nothing; for Lenard-Balescu it returns a NamedTuple of dielectric and k-space precomputations.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.precompute_dielectric_data","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.precompute_dielectric_data","text":"precompute_dielectric_data(r, f_prime, dim=2, nang=16;\n                           radial_symmetry=true, f=nothing, grid=nothing,\n                           rho_points_3d=0, psi_points_3d=0)\n\nPrecompute G(x) and H[G](x) for efficient dielectric response calculation.\n\nComputes once:\n\nG(x) = S{d-2} ∫{|x|}^{∞} f'(r) (r²-x²)^{(d-3)/2} dr\nH[G](x) = Hilbert transform of G\nI = ∫_0^∞ f'(r) r^{d-2} dr\n\nArguments\n\nr: Radial grid for distribution (radial_symmetry=true path; otherwise nothing)\nf_prime: Distribution derivative on radial grid (radial_symmetry=true path; otherwise nothing)\ndim: Dimension (2 or 3)\nnang: Angular sampling count for generic (non-radial) mode\nradial_symmetry: Select radial (true) or generic (false) dielectric preprocessing\nf: Reconstructed distribution on velocity grid (required in generic mode)\ngrid: Velocity-grid coordinate tuple used in generic mode ((Vx, Vy) or (Vx, Vy, Vz))\nrho_points_3d, psi_points_3d: Optional 3D non-radial quadrature resolutions\n\nReturns\n\nG: G values on extended grid\nHG: Hilbert[G] values on extended grid\nr_ext: Extended radial grid [-L, ..., L]\nI_integral: Normalization integral used in radial mode\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.precompute_dielectric_lookup_grid-Tuple{Params, AbstractArray{Float64}}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.precompute_dielectric_lookup_grid","text":"precompute_dielectric_lookup_grid(par, Vgrid; radial_symmetry=true)\n\nPrecompute fixed interpolation-grid metadata used by fused Lenard-Balescu kernels: (r0, dr, inv_dr, len).\n\nThis depends on grid geometry (par, Vgrid, radial_symmetry) and can be computed once per simulation run.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.precompute_k_space-Tuple{Int64, Float64, Float64, Int64}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.precompute_k_space","text":"precompute_k_space(k_perp_order::Int, k_perp_max::Float64, k_parallel_width::Float64, k_parallel_order::Int)\n\nPrecompute 2D k-space grid and weights matching MATLAB reference:\n\nGauss-Legendre in kperp on [-kperpmax, kperp_max]\nHat function approximation for delta in kparallel on [-kparallelwidth, kparallel_width]\n\nArguments\n\nk_perp_order: Number of Gauss-Legendre quadrature points for k_perp (resolution)\nk_perp_max: Maximum k_perp value (integration range)\nk_parallel_width: Hat-delta width for k_parallel (delta function approximation)\nk_parallel_order: Number of points for k_parallel (resolution of delta approximation)\n\nReturns\n\nk_parallel, k_perp, norm_k, approx, phi_p_11, phi_p_22, phi_p_12, k_angle_local\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.precompute_k_space_3d-Tuple{Int64, Float64, Float64, Int64}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.precompute_k_space_3d","text":"precompute_k_space_3d(k_perp_order, k_perp_max, k_parallel_width, k_parallel_order)\n\nPrecompute 3D k-space samples in a local frame (k_parallel, k_perp2, k_perp3). The two perpendicular directions use Gauss-Legendre quadrature and k_parallel uses the same hat-delta approximation as the 2D implementation.\n\nk_perp_order is used directly as the quadrature order in each perpendicular direction (k_perp2, k_perp3).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.projected_line_points-Tuple{Float64, Float64, Int64}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.projected_line_points","text":"projected_line_points(r_extent::Float64, dv_par::Float64, Nv::Int) -> Int\n\nCompute the number of points for the projected parallel velocity line used in non-radial dielectric precomputation.\n\nEnsures that the line from -r_extent to r_extent is sampled at least as densely as the underlying velocity grid (spacing dv_par), and always returns an odd count so that the grid is symmetric about zero.\n\nArguments\n\nr_extent: Half-length of the projected line (maximum particle speed on grid).\ndv_par: Target parallel grid spacing (typically the minimum axis spacing).\nNv: Minimum number of points (usually the grid resolution per axis).\n\nReturns\n\nNumber of sample points (odd integer, ≥ Nv).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.read_vector_csv-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.read_vector_csv","text":"read_vector_csv(path::AbstractString)\n\nRead a vector of Float64 values from a CSV file.\n\nArguments\n\npath: Path to the CSV file.\n\nReturns\n\nA vector of Float64 values read from the file.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.safe_e-Tuple{BasisKernel}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.safe_e","text":"safe_e(k::BasisKernel)\n\nLower-bound the kernel scale parameter to avoid numerical issues when e is too small.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.update_kernel_params!-Tuple{Params}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.update_kernel_params!","text":"update_kernel_params!(par::Params)\n\nUpdate the derived kernel parameters (cell_h and epsi) in a Params struct based on the current grid and spline settings.\n\nArguments\n\npar: The Params struct to update (modified in-place).\n\nReturns\n\nThe updated Params struct (same object, for convenience).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"api/#LenardBalescu.write_vector_csv-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractVector{<:Real}}","page":"API","title":"LenardBalescu.write_vector_csv","text":"write_vector_csv(fname::AbstractString, v::AbstractVector{<:Real}; dir::AbstractString=\"../data\")\n\nWrite a vector of real numbers to a CSV file.\n\nArguments\n\nfname: Name of the CSV file to write.\nv: Vector of real numbers to write.\ndir: Directory to save the file (default: \"../data\").\n\nReturns\n\nThe full path to the written CSV file as a string.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"license/","page":"-","title":"-","text":"MIT License\n\nCopyright (c) 2026 Timon S. Gutleb\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/3d-torus/#3D-Torus-walkthrough","page":"Examples/3D Torus","title":"3D Torus walkthrough","text":"This page is a walkthrough of examples/3D_run_lenardbalescu_demo_torus.jl. It explains what the script does, in order, and how to modify it.","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/3d-torus/#What-this-example-is","page":"Examples/3D Torus","title":"What this example is","text":"Operator: 3D Lenard–Balescu (use_lenard_balescu=true)\nSymmetry mode: non-radial (radial_symmetry=false)\nInitial condition: torus in velocity space (initialize_particles_torus_3d)\nEntry point function: run_lenardbalescu_demo_3d_torus_nonradial\n\nAt the bottom of the script, this function is called directly, so running the file starts a simulation immediately.","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/3d-torus/#Step-1-—-Run-it-as-provided","page":"Examples/3D Torus","title":"Step 1 — Run it as provided","text":"From the repository root:\n\njulia --project -e 'include(\"examples/3D_run_lenardbalescu_demo_torus.jl\")'\n\nThis executes the function call at the bottom of the script (currently a long run with ntot=500).","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/3d-torus/#Step-2-—-Understand-the-flow-inside-the-function","page":"Examples/3D Torus","title":"Step 2 — Understand the flow inside the function","text":"run_lenardbalescu_demo_3d_torus_nonradial does the following:\n\nCreates RNG and parameters (rng = MersenneTwister(seed), par = SetParam()).\nSets 3D discretization/time controls (par.dim, par.Nv, par.Npc, par.dt, par.ntot, par.T).\nSets Lenard–Balescu k-space controls (k_perp_order, k_perp_max, k_parallel_width, k_parallel_order).\nSets basis choice (par.spline_order = 0) and Gaussian support (par.gaussian_cutoff_sigma).\nCreates output directories and animation objects.\nDefines a per-step callback that:\nsamples particles for plotting,\nbuilds static and rotating 3D scatter frames,\noptionally builds a 3×3 combined diagnostics panel.\nCalls run_simulation(...) with:\ntorus initializer: initialize_particles_torus_3d(...),\ndiagnostics enabled: savecsv=true, trackconserved=true,\ncallback attached for animation/diagnostics.\nWrites GIFs and summary plots to the configured output paths.","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/3d-torus/#Step-3-—-Run-a-shorter/faster-variant-interactively","page":"Examples/3D Torus","title":"Step 3 — Run a shorter/faster variant interactively","text":"For quick iteration, call the function yourself with smaller settings:\n\nusing LenardBalescu\ninclude(\"examples/3D_run_lenardbalescu_demo_torus.jl\")\n\nrun_lenardbalescu_demo_3d_torus_nonradial(\n\t ntot=40,\n\t seed=1,\n\t batchsize=300,\n\t make_animation=false,\n\t make_combined_evolution=false,\n\t make_plots=true\n)","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/3d-torus/#Step-4-—-What-to-modify-(and-what-each-knob-changes)","page":"Examples/3D Torus","title":"Step 4 — What to modify (and what each knob changes)","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/3d-torus/#Geometry-and-initialization","page":"Examples/3D Torus","title":"Geometry and initialization","text":"major_radius: moves torus ring outward/inward in velocity space.\ntube_radius: changes torus thickness.\nInitializer is defined in init_particles=(...) -> initialize_particles_torus_3d(...).","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/3d-torus/#Runtime-and-cost","page":"Examples/3D Torus","title":"Runtime and cost","text":"ntot: number of timesteps (largest runtime lever).\nbatchsize: RBM batching size in run_simulation; lower than N enables random batching and usually speeds up runs.\npar.Nv, par.Npc: particle count/discretization; increasing either increases cost.","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/3d-torus/#Lenard–Balescu-fidelity-controls","page":"Examples/3D Torus","title":"Lenard–Balescu fidelity controls","text":"par.k_perp_order, par.k_perp_max, par.k_parallel_width, par.k_parallel_order.\nHigher quadrature/order is typically more accurate but slower.","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/3d-torus/#Output-and-visualization","page":"Examples/3D Torus","title":"Output and visualization","text":"make_animation, make_combined_evolution, make_plots toggle output products.\nmax_anim_particles controls plotting subsampling.\nanim_fps, rotate_turns control animation style.\nout_dir, out_gif, out_gif_rotating, out_gif_combined control file locations.","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/3d-torus/#Practical-notes","page":"Examples/3D Torus","title":"Practical notes","text":"The script currently auto-runs at the bottom. If you want library-style usage only, remove or comment out that last call and invoke the function manually.\nOutput files are written under examples/output/lenard_balescu_3d_torus_nonradial/ by default.","category":"section"},{"location":"#LenardBalescu.jl","page":"Home","title":"LenardBalescu.jl","text":"A Julia package for 3D and 2D multi-threaded plasma simulations using particle-in-cell methods with the Lenard–Balescu or Landau collision operators. This project is under active development and is not yet registered.","category":"section"},{"location":"#Installation","page":"Home","title":"Installation","text":"Install directly from the repository:\n\nusing Pkg\nPkg.add(url=\"https://github.com/TSGut/LenardBalescu.jl\")","category":"section"},{"location":"#Quick-start","page":"Home","title":"Quick start","text":"using LenardBalescu\n\npar = SetParam()          # default parameters\nresult = run_simulation(; par, use_lenard_balescu=true, verbose=1)","category":"section"},{"location":"#Examples","page":"Home","title":"Examples","text":"The examples/ directory contains runnable demos and helper scripts. Some examples also have additional walkthrough-style docs:\n\n2D Elliptical BKW walkthrough\n3D Torus walkthrough","category":"section"},{"location":"#Benchmarks","page":"Home","title":"Benchmarks","text":"Benchmark and profiling scripts live in benchmarks/. Notable scripts:\n\n2D_benchmark_complexity_N.jl, 3D_benchmark_complexity_N.jl — complexity vs number of particles\n2D_benchmark_complexity_kperp.jl, 3D_benchmark_complexity_kperp.jl — complexity vs k_perp_order\n2D_benchmark_complexity_nang.jl, 3D_benchmark_complexity_nang.jl — non-radial dielectric angular sampling\n2D_benchmark_profile_lenardbalescu_bkw.jl, 3D_benchmark_profile_lenardbalescu_maxwell.jl — profiling runs\n2D_benchmark_threading.jl, 3D_benchmark_threading.jl — thread-scaling benchmarks\n\nRun benchmarks from the benchmarks/ directory; outputs are written to benchmarks/output/ or shown on the console depending on the script.","category":"section"},{"location":"#License","page":"Home","title":"License","text":"MIT — see LICENSE.","category":"section"}]
}
